[h2]Fluid network update[/h2]
Bounded multi-receiver port banks retain the original single-pair identity. Reusable retained two-component fluid lines preserve cargo, route binding and transit clocks across reloads.

[h2]Equipment and item reference[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/framework-item-reference.md]Read this mod’s item reference[/url] for functions, use, acquisition and applicable base prices, repair and salvage. Generated tables follow the current source candidate; proposals and prototype limitations are labelled.

[h2]Nutrient recovery and optional wet-reject collection[/h2]
Optional Agriculture 0.9.0 integration reuses the original Residue Collector with finite capacity, exclusive pairing and its existing mount requirements. Framework 0.22.0 and Shipbreaker 0.20.0 support measured wet-reject capture from [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3757331189]Valtora’s Ship’s Water 0.16.1[/url]. Full or unavailable linked collectors hold wastewater in its source tank. No wastewater-to-fertilizer recipe is claimed. [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/agriculture-nutrient-production.md]Operating guide, economic limits and research attribution[/url].

[h2]Bulk merchant stock[/h2]
Quantity-aware merchant and regional-stock overloads request bounded physical lots while retaining the old single-unit API. Probability and stock condition remain independent; native and third-party branches and existing inventories are preserved.
Normal restocking is required; updating does not refill existing shops. [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/merchant-stock.md]Current quantities and restocking guide[/url]. Prepared candidate; in-game stock/capacity review pending.
